{% doc %}
  Size Guide — designed from scratch around THE TAPE (Sep 2026, owner's
  direction).

  The tape comes FIRST: one continuous 8-loop tailor's tape
  (Higgsfield-generated, background-removed, natural ends — a metal tab at
  both tips, so nothing is ever cut mid-ribbon) laid at its own
  proportions inside an aspect-locked canvas. Every text block is then
  placed into the loops' EMPTY GAPS — measured off the image itself — so
  copy can never sit on the ribbon. Cut-out imagery may layer beside or
  over the bands; the frock with the chest tape anchors to the viewport's
  right edge so its tape end leaves the frame. The chart (an opaque card)
  and the WhatsApp hand-off follow below the tape's end.

  Desktop is the composed canvas; under 880px the canvas unstacks into a
  plain column and the tape steps aside.
{% enddoc %}

{%- liquid
  assign whatsapp = shop.metafields.custom.whatsapp_number.value
-%}

<section class="sv-sg" data-sv>

  {%- render 'sv-motion-gate' -%}

  <div class="sv-sg__canvas">
    {%- comment -%} The tape, first. Everything else fits around it. {%- endcomment -%}
    <img class="sv-sg__tape" src="{{ 'sv-sg-longtape.png' | asset_url }}" alt="" aria-hidden="true" width="1451" height="2600" loading="eager">

    <header class="sv-sg__blk sv-sg__head" data-sv-motion>
      <p class="eyebrow">Our size guide</p>
      <h1 class="sv-sg__title">Measured<br>with <em>care.</em></h1>
      <p class="sv-sg__lead">Children of the same age can be very different sizes, so please do not order by age alone. The most reliable method takes two minutes and a garment your child already loves.</p>
    </header>

    <div class="sv-sg__blk sv-sg__s1" data-sv-motion>
      <span class="num" aria-hidden="true">01</span>
      <p class="eyebrow">Lay it flat</p>
      <p>Take a garment your child already wears comfortably and lay it out flat on a table.</p>
    </div>
    <img class="sv-sg__img sv-sg__img1" data-sv-motion src="{{ 'sv-sg-stack.png' | asset_url }}" alt="" width="900" height="900" loading="lazy">

    <div class="sv-sg__blk sv-sg__s2" data-sv-motion>
      <span class="num" aria-hidden="true">02</span>
      <p class="eyebrow">The chest</p>
      <p>Measure across, from armpit to armpit, and double it. That is the chest measurement.</p>
    </div>
    {%- comment -%} The frock at the right end: its tape runs off-frame. {%- endcomment -%}
    <img class="sv-sg__img sv-sg__img2" data-sv-motion src="{{ 'sv-sg-chest.png' | asset_url }}" alt="" width="1000" height="746" loading="lazy">

    <div class="sv-sg__blk sv-sg__s3" data-sv-motion>
      <span class="num" aria-hidden="true">03</span>
      <p class="eyebrow">The length</p>
      <p>Measure from the highest point of the shoulder straight down to the hem. That is the length.</p>
    </div>

    <div class="sv-sg__blk sv-sg__s4" data-sv-motion>
      <span class="num" aria-hidden="true">04</span>
      <p class="eyebrow">Match the chart</p>
      <p>Match both numbers to the chart below and pick the nearest size up — between two sizes, always go one up.</p>
    </div>
    <img class="sv-sg__img sv-sg__img4" data-sv-motion src="{{ 'sv-sg-tags.png' | asset_url }}" alt="" width="900" height="900" loading="lazy">
    {%- comment -%} A second set of labels at the left edge, beside 03. {%- endcomment -%}
    <img class="sv-sg__img sv-sg__img5" data-sv-motion src="{{ 'sv-sg-tags.png' | asset_url }}" alt="" width="900" height="900" loading="lazy">

    <div class="sv-sg__blk sv-sg__chart" data-sv-motion>
      <h2 class="sv-sg__h2">The size chart</h2>
      <table>
        <thead>
          <tr><th>Size</th><th>Age</th><th>Chest (cm)</th><th>Garment length (cm)</th></tr>
        </thead>
        <tbody>
          <tr><td>S1</td><td>0–6 months</td><td>44–46</td><td>36–38</td></tr>
          <tr><td>S2</td><td>6–12 months</td><td>47–49</td><td>39–41</td></tr>
          <tr><td>S3</td><td>1–2 years</td><td>50–52</td><td>42–45</td></tr>
          <tr><td>S4</td><td>2–3 years</td><td>53–55</td><td>46–49</td></tr>
          <tr><td>S5</td><td>3–4 years</td><td>56–58</td><td>50–53</td></tr>
          <tr><td>S6</td><td>4–5 years</td><td>59–61</td><td>54–57</td></tr>
          <tr><td>S7</td><td>5–6 years</td><td>62–64</td><td>58–61</td></tr>
          <tr><td>S8</td><td>6–7 years</td><td>65–68</td><td>62–65</td></tr>
          <tr><td>S9</td><td>7–8 years</td><td>69–72</td><td>66–69</td></tr>
        </tbody>
      </table>
      <p class="sv-sg__note"><em>Measurements are of the garment laid flat, not of the body, and may vary by 1–2 cm between styles. Every product page carries the exact chart for that garment — always check it before ordering.</em></p>
    </div>

    <div class="sv-sg__blk sv-sg__unsure" data-sv-motion>
      <h2 class="sv-sg__h2">Still unsure?</h2>
      <p>Send us your child&rsquo;s chest and height measurement on WhatsApp at
        {%- if whatsapp != blank %}
        <a class="sv-sg__walink" href="https://wa.me/{{ whatsapp }}?text=Hi%20Sahasra%20Vastra%2C%20my%20child%27s%20chest%20is%20__%20cm%20and%20height%20__%20cm.%20Which%20size%20should%20I%20order%3F" rel="noopener" target="_blank">+91 85476 29251</a>
        {%- else %} +91 85476 29251{% endif %}
        and we will tell you which size to order.</p>
      {%- if whatsapp != blank -%}
        <a class="btn sv-sg__cta" href="https://wa.me/{{ whatsapp }}?text=Hi%20Sahasra%20Vastra%2C%20my%20child%27s%20chest%20is%20__%20cm%20and%20height%20__%20cm.%20Which%20size%20should%20I%20order%3F" rel="noopener" target="_blank">Ask on WhatsApp</a>
      {%- endif -%}
    </div>
  </div>

  {%- comment -%}
    Motion driver. sv-motion.js reveals ONCE and unobserves, so nothing
    replayed on a second pass; this observer keeps watching and toggles
    the state every crossing, which is what makes the page move whenever
    you scroll — down AND back up. IntersectionObserver only: no scroll
    listeners, per the theme's performance rule.
  {%- endcomment -%}
  <script>
    (() => {
      const root = document.currentScript.closest('.sv-sg');
      if (!root) return;
      const targets = root.querySelectorAll('[data-sv-motion]');
      /* The hidden state only exists once JS is here to undo it, so a
         failed script leaves the page fully readable. */
      root.classList.add('sv-motion-ready');
      if (matchMedia('(prefers-reduced-motion: reduce)').matches) {
        targets.forEach(el => el.classList.add('sv-vis'));
        return;
      }
      const io = new IntersectionObserver(entries => {
        entries.forEach(e => e.target.classList.toggle('sv-vis', e.isIntersecting));
      }, { threshold: 0.14, rootMargin: '-4% 0px -10% 0px' });
      targets.forEach(el => io.observe(el));

      /* Fail-safe. A tab loaded in the background defers observer
         callbacks, which would leave whatever is on screen sitting at
         opacity 0. Anything actually within the viewport shortly after
         load is shown outright; the observer still governs it from then
         on, so nothing is ever stranded blank. */
      setTimeout(() => {
        targets.forEach(el => {
          const r = el.getBoundingClientRect();
          if (r.top < innerHeight && r.bottom > 0) el.classList.add('sv-vis');
        });
      }, 1200);
    })();
  </script>
</section>

{% stylesheet %}
  /* Colour and spacing are tokens only; type comes from sv-system.css
     primitives (.eyebrow, .num, .btn, serif headings under [data-sv]). */
  [data-sv].sv-sg {
    position: relative;
    /* clip, not hidden: `hidden` makes this a scroll container and left
       every view() timeline inside it inactive. */
    overflow: clip;
    padding: var(--c) 0 var(--b);
    background:
      radial-gradient(640px 420px at 85% 4%, rgba(198, 161, 91, 0.10), transparent 70%),
      radial-gradient(720px 520px at 6% 60%, rgba(20, 82, 74, 0.05), transparent 70%),
      var(--cream);
  }

  /* ── the canvas ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────
     Locked to the tape's own 1451:2600 proportions, so every block placed
     in a gap STAYS in that gap at any viewport width. Block coordinates
     below are percentages measured off the tape image itself. */
  /* container-type: text inside sizes in cqw, so type shrinks WITH the
     canvas and blocks stay inside their loops at every desktop width. */
  .sv-sg__canvas {
    --sv-canvas-w: min(1400px, 97vw);
    position: relative;
    width: var(--sv-canvas-w);
    margin-inline: auto;
    aspect-ratio: 1451 / 2600;
    container-type: inline-size;
    /* The canvas ends ~8.3% of its width below the last line of copy —
       blank tape-less ground. Pulled up so the footer follows the
       content, not the empty box; the section's overflow clips it. */
    margin-bottom: calc(var(--sv-canvas-w) * -0.083);
  }

  .sv-sg__tape {
    position: absolute;
    inset: 0;
    width: 100%;
    height: 100%;
    opacity: 0.9;
    /* multiply melts the PNG's white halo fringe into the cream ground */
    mix-blend-mode: multiply;
    pointer-events: none;
    /* The image's dangling 1-8 strip at the frock's row is masked out —
       a rectangular hole over it (two layers, second subtracted), sized
       to spare the main ribbon passing down the right side. */
    -webkit-mask-image: linear-gradient(180deg, #000 65%, transparent 69%), linear-gradient(#000 0 0);
    -webkit-mask-size: 100% 100%, 74% 5.5%;
    -webkit-mask-position: 0 0, 0 30.5%;
    -webkit-mask-repeat: no-repeat;
    -webkit-mask-composite: xor;
    /* The first layer now fades the ribbon out below the chart: the stub
       beside the hand-off and the closing sweep above the footer both go
       with it. The other two layers stay as their local cut-outs. */
    mask-image: linear-gradient(180deg, #000 65%, transparent 69%), linear-gradient(#000 0 0);
    mask-size: 100% 100%, 74% 5.5%;
    mask-position: 0 0, 0 30.5%;
    mask-repeat: no-repeat;
    mask-composite: exclude;
  }

  .sv-sg__blk {
    position: absolute;
    z-index: 1;
  }

  .sv-sg__img {
    position: absolute;
    z-index: 1;
    height: auto;
    filter: drop-shadow(0 18px 30px rgba(26, 26, 26, 0.13));
  }

  /* ── the gaps, block by block ─────────────────────────────────────── */
  .sv-sg__head { left: 3%; top: 1.2%; width: 48%; }

  [data-sv] .sv-sg__title {
    font-size: clamp(2.1rem, 4.6cqw, 4.4rem);
    margin-top: var(--a);
  }

  .sv-sg__title em {
    font-style: italic;
    color: var(--tan);
  }

  /* Readability pass (owner): ink instead of warm grey, regular weight
     instead of the body's 300, and a higher size floor — the canvas copy
     is small and often near the tape, so it gets no room to be faint. */
  .sv-sg__lead {
    margin-top: var(--a);
    color: var(--ink);
    font-weight: 400;
    max-width: 42ch;
    font-size: clamp(0.9rem, 1.45cqw, 1.18rem);
    line-height: 1.65;
  }

  /* Number and label share a line: the flatter block is what keeps a
     whole stop inside its loop at every canvas width. */
  .sv-sg__blk .num {
    display: inline-block;
    vertical-align: baseline;
    margin-right: 12px;
    font-size: clamp(1.8rem, 3.6cqw, 3.3rem);
    /* .num ships at 0.5 opacity — too faint over this composition. */
    opacity: 0.85;
  }
  /* Eyebrows across the canvas — the head's OUR SIZE GUIDE included —
     read a step larger, per the owner. */
  .sv-sg__canvas .eyebrow {
    font-size: clamp(0.95rem, 1.5cqw, 1.2rem);
    font-weight: 600;
    color: var(--ink);
  }

  .sv-sg__blk .eyebrow {
    display: inline-flex;
    vertical-align: baseline;
    margin-block: 0;
  }
  .sv-sg__blk > p:last-child {
    color: var(--ink);
    font-weight: 400;
    font-size: clamp(0.9rem, 1.45cqw, 1.18rem);
    line-height: 1.65;
    margin-top: 10px;
  }

  .sv-sg__s1 { left: 20.5%; top: 15.8%; width: 25%; }
  .sv-sg__img1 {
    left: auto;
    right: calc((100% - 100vw) / 2 + 24px);
    top: 5.8%;
    width: 25%;
  }

  .sv-sg__s2 { left: 8%; top: 28.9%; width: 32%; }
  /* The frock, at the right end: anchored to the viewport edge so the
     chest tape's raw end leaves the frame. */
  .sv-sg__img2 {
    right: calc((100% - 100vw) / 2);
    top: 23.8%;
    width: 46%;
    /* The chest tape's overhang past the dress fades out — the ribbon
       reads as continuing, never as cut. */
    -webkit-mask-image: linear-gradient(90deg, #000 79%, transparent 86%);
    mask-image: linear-gradient(90deg, #000 79%, transparent 86%);
  }

  .sv-sg__s3 { left: 21%; top: 45.2%; width: 23%; }

  .sv-sg__s4 { left: 53%; top: 54.9%; width: 30%; }
  .sv-sg__img4 { left: 74%; top: 63.5%; width: 22%; }

  .sv-sg__img5 {
    left: calc((100% - 100vw) / 2 + 36px);
    top: 52.6%;
    width: 19%;
    transform: rotate(-12deg);
  }


  /* ── chart: an opaque card over the tape's lower reach ────────────── */
  .sv-sg__chart { left: 3%; top: 67.4%; width: 55%; }

  [data-sv] .sv-sg__h2 {
    font-size: clamp(1.5rem, 2.4vw, 2rem);
    color: var(--emerald);
    margin-bottom: var(--a);
  }

  .sv-sg__canvas .sv-sg__h2 {
    font-size: clamp(1.4rem, 2.6cqw, 2.5rem);
  }

  .sv-sg__chart table {
    width: 100%;
    border-collapse: collapse;
    background: var(--card);
    box-shadow: var(--sh-s);
    border-radius: var(--r-img);
    overflow: hidden;
  }

  .sv-sg__chart th {
    font-family: var(--sans);
    font-weight: 400;
    font-size: clamp(0.62rem, 1cqw, 0.8rem);
    letter-spacing: 0.16em;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    text-align: left;
    color: var(--cream);
    background: var(--emerald);
    padding: 10px 14px;
  }

  .sv-sg__chart td {
    padding: clamp(6px, 0.85cqw, 11px) clamp(10px, 1.3cqw, 16px);
    font-size: clamp(0.85rem, 1.35cqw, 1.08rem);
    border-bottom: 1px solid var(--cream-2);
  }

  .sv-sg__chart tbody tr:last-child td { border-bottom: 0; }
  .sv-sg__chart tbody tr:nth-child(even) td { background: var(--cream); }

  /* The note sits on its own wash: a band passes beneath it and text
     never reads off the ribbon. */
  .sv-sg__note {
    position: relative;
    margin-top: 12.25cqw;
    color: var(--ink);
    font-size: clamp(0.82rem, 1.3cqw, 1.02rem);
    padding: 10px 14px;
  }

  /* The tape is hidden behind these two blocks rather than masked out of
     the image: a cream wash, blurred so it has no edge of its own. On the
     cream ground it is invisible; over the ribbon it blots it out, and it
     follows the copy at every width instead of being a fixed cut-out. */
  .sv-sg__note::before,
  .sv-sg__unsure::before {
    content: '';
    position: absolute;
    inset: -18px -26px;
    z-index: -1;
    background: var(--cream);
    filter: blur(14px);
    pointer-events: none;
  }

  .sv-sg__unsure::before {
    inset: -26px -34px;
  }

  .sv-sg__note em {
    font-family: var(--serif);
    font-size: 1.05em;
  }

  /* ── the hand-off, in the clear zone beside the chart ─────────────── */
  .sv-sg__unsure {
    left: 61%;
    top: 79%;
    width: 33%;
    text-align: center;
  }

  .sv-sg__unsure p {
    margin-inline: auto;
    color: var(--ink);
  }

  .sv-sg__walink {
    color: var(--emerald);
    text-decoration: underline;
    text-underline-offset: 0.25em;
    text-decoration-color: var(--tan);
    white-space: nowrap;
  }

  .sv-sg__cta {
    margin-top: var(--b);
  }


  /* ── MOTION ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────
     Every effect keys off .sv-vis, which the observer above toggles on
     EVERY crossing — so the page animates each time it is scrolled, in
     both directions, not just on first load. Opacity and `translate`
     only (never `transform`), so the rotated label set keeps its angle. */
  @media (prefers-reduced-motion: no-preference) {
    .sv-sg.sv-motion-ready [data-sv-motion] {
      transition:
        opacity 0.7s var(--entrance),
        translate 0.7s var(--entrance),
        filter 0.7s var(--entrance);
    }

    /* Resting (out of view) — copy waits below, objects a little lower
       still and flatter, so they settle rather than slide. */
    .sv-sg.sv-motion-ready .sv-sg__blk:not(.sv-vis) {
      opacity: 0;
      translate: 0 30px;
    }

    .sv-sg.sv-motion-ready .sv-sg__img:not(.sv-vis) {
      opacity: 0;
      translate: 0 40px;
      filter: drop-shadow(0 4px 8px rgba(26, 26, 26, 0.05));
    }

    .sv-sg.sv-motion-ready [data-sv-motion].sv-vis {
      opacity: 1;
      translate: 0 0;
    }

    /* Three beats per stop: the numeral, then the dash with its label,
       then the copy — replayed on every pass. */
    .sv-sg.sv-motion-ready .sv-sg__blk .num,
    .sv-sg.sv-motion-ready .sv-sg__blk .eyebrow,
    .sv-sg.sv-motion-ready .sv-sg__blk .sv-sg__title,
    .sv-sg.sv-motion-ready .sv-sg__blk .sv-sg__lead,
    .sv-sg.sv-motion-ready .sv-sg__blk > p:last-child {
      transition: opacity 0.55s var(--entrance), translate 0.55s var(--entrance);
    }

    .sv-sg.sv-motion-ready .sv-sg__blk:not(.sv-vis) .num { opacity: 0; translate: 0 0.4em; }
    .sv-sg.sv-motion-ready .sv-sg__blk:not(.sv-vis) .eyebrow { opacity: 0; translate: -12px 0; }
    .sv-sg.sv-motion-ready .sv-sg__blk:not(.sv-vis) .sv-sg__title { opacity: 0; translate: 0 16px; }
    .sv-sg.sv-motion-ready .sv-sg__blk:not(.sv-vis) .sv-sg__lead,
    .sv-sg.sv-motion-ready .sv-sg__blk:not(.sv-vis) > p:last-child { opacity: 0; translate: 0 12px; }

    .sv-sg.sv-motion-ready .sv-sg__blk.sv-vis .eyebrow { transition-delay: 0.16s; }
    .sv-sg.sv-motion-ready .sv-sg__blk.sv-vis .sv-sg__title { transition-delay: 0.12s; }
    .sv-sg.sv-motion-ready .sv-sg__blk.sv-vis .sv-sg__lead,
    .sv-sg.sv-motion-ready .sv-sg__blk.sv-vis > p:last-child { transition-delay: 0.3s; }

    /* The dash draws itself in. */
    .sv-sg.sv-motion-ready .sv-sg__blk .eyebrow::before {
      transform-origin: left center;
      transition: transform 0.5s var(--entrance) 0.16s;
    }
    .sv-sg.sv-motion-ready .sv-sg__blk:not(.sv-vis) .eyebrow::before { transform: scaleX(0); }

    /* Chart: heading first, the nine rows cascade, the note closes. */
    .sv-sg.sv-motion-ready .sv-sg__chart .sv-sg__h2,
    .sv-sg.sv-motion-ready .sv-sg__chart .sv-sg__note,
    .sv-sg.sv-motion-ready .sv-sg__chart tbody tr {
      transition: opacity 0.5s var(--entrance), translate 0.5s var(--entrance);
    }

    .sv-sg.sv-motion-ready .sv-sg__chart:not(.sv-vis) .sv-sg__h2 { opacity: 0; translate: 0 10px; }
    .sv-sg.sv-motion-ready .sv-sg__chart:not(.sv-vis) .sv-sg__note { opacity: 0; }
    .sv-sg.sv-motion-ready .sv-sg__chart:not(.sv-vis) tbody tr { opacity: 0; translate: -10px 0; }

    .sv-sg.sv-motion-ready .sv-sg__chart.sv-vis tbody tr:nth-child(1) { transition-delay: 0.10s; }
    .sv-sg.sv-motion-ready .sv-sg__chart.sv-vis tbody tr:nth-child(2) { transition-delay: 0.15s; }
    .sv-sg.sv-motion-ready .sv-sg__chart.sv-vis tbody tr:nth-child(3) { transition-delay: 0.20s; }
    .sv-sg.sv-motion-ready .sv-sg__chart.sv-vis tbody tr:nth-child(4) { transition-delay: 0.25s; }
    .sv-sg.sv-motion-ready .sv-sg__chart.sv-vis tbody tr:nth-child(5) { transition-delay: 0.30s; }
    .sv-sg.sv-motion-ready .sv-sg__chart.sv-vis tbody tr:nth-child(6) { transition-delay: 0.35s; }
    .sv-sg.sv-motion-ready .sv-sg__chart.sv-vis tbody tr:nth-child(7) { transition-delay: 0.40s; }
    .sv-sg.sv-motion-ready .sv-sg__chart.sv-vis tbody tr:nth-child(8) { transition-delay: 0.45s; }
    .sv-sg.sv-motion-ready .sv-sg__chart.sv-vis tbody tr:nth-child(9) { transition-delay: 0.50s; }
    .sv-sg.sv-motion-ready .sv-sg__chart.sv-vis .sv-sg__note { transition-delay: 0.62s; }

    /* The hand-off rings once each time it arrives. */
    .sv-sg.sv-motion-ready .sv-sg__unsure.sv-vis .sv-sg__cta {
      animation: sv-sg-cta 1s var(--e) 0.7s 1 both;
    }

    @keyframes sv-sg-cta {
      0% { box-shadow: 0 0 0 0 rgba(20, 82, 74, 0.35); }
      100% { box-shadow: 0 0 0 18px rgba(20, 82, 74, 0); }
    }

    /* Scroll-linked, and therefore continuous in both directions: the
       tape unrolls with the scroll and the objects drift against it. */
    @supports (animation-timeline: view()) {
      .sv-sg__tape {
        animation: sv-sg-unroll linear both;
        animation-timeline: view();
        animation-range: cover 0% cover 70%;
      }

      @keyframes sv-sg-unroll {
        from { clip-path: inset(-2% -2% 102% -2%); }
        to { clip-path: inset(-2% -2% -2% -2%); }
      }
    }
  }

  /* ── under 880px the canvas unstacks into a plain column ──────────── */
  @media (max-width: 879px) {
    .sv-sg__canvas {
      width: auto;
      aspect-ratio: auto;
      margin-bottom: 0;
      margin-inline: var(--b);
      display: flex;
      flex-direction: column;
      gap: var(--b);
    }

    .sv-sg__tape {
      display: none;
    }

    .sv-sg__blk,
    .sv-sg__img {
      position: static;
      width: auto;
    }

    .sv-sg__img {
      width: min(320px, 84%);
      align-self: center;
    }

    .sv-sg__img2 {
      align-self: flex-end;
      margin-right: calc(-1 * var(--b));
      width: min(420px, 96%);
    }

    /* One set of labels is enough in the stacked column. */
    .sv-sg__img5 {
      display: none;
    }

    .sv-sg__head {
      margin-block: var(--b) var(--a);
    }

    /* Static column again: give type its normal size back. */
    .sv-sg__lead,
    .sv-sg__blk > p:last-child { font-size: 0.95rem; }
    .sv-sg__blk .num { font-size: 2rem; }
